# Keep the Docker build context small and reproducible: dependencies are
# installed inside the image, and local build output or secrets must not leak in.
# Build-time config reaches the image only through build args (see the ARG/ENV
# lines in the Dockerfile). Local env files, at any depth, are deliberately not
# copied, so they never enter the build context; only the .env.example template
# is kept, so never put real values in it. Build-arg values can still persist in
# builder metadata or cache, so do not pass real secrets that way.
.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
dist
web-build
.expo
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!.env.example
ios
android
src-tauri/target
**/*.log
.DS_Store
